    "CSCI-401 (Capstone) is placed in Semester 2 (the final semester) per capstone timing rules; it requires CSCI-310 which is placed in Semester 1, satisfying the prereq ordering constraint.",
    "CSCI-485 (File and Database Management) is selected as the top-ranked elective (score 1.0) to satisfy the 4-unit upper-division elective budget; all prereqs are already in the completed timeline.",
    "TAC-303 (Full-Stack Web Development) is placed in Semester 2 as enrichment — it is the top-ranked enrichment course (score 1.0) and directly aligns with the backend engineering career goal. Its prereq (CSCI-103) is already in the completed timeline. TAC-405 (Advanced Back-End Web Development), which depends on TAC-303, cannot be placed in the same semester and would require a third semester, which would push the plan over the minimum-semester constraint given the 12–18 unit load; TAC-303 alone is placed as the highest-value enrichment that fits."
